  "question": {
    "text": "The below plot shows the variation of binding energy per nucleon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>b</mi></msub></math>, against the nuclear mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math>. The different points shown <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math>&nbsp;correspond to different nuclei. In which of the following reactions, the energy released&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>Q</mi></mfenced></math> will be positive?<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/Questions654849.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 105px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
